title: 'FRAME: point macro diagnostics at offending declarations'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Compiler errors when encoding pallet constants now highlight the associated type or
    extra-constant function responsible for the error, rather than the outer pallet attribute.
    Tuple-struct DebugNoBound, CloneNoBound, PartialEqNoBound, PartialOrdNoBound, and OrdNoBound
    derives preserve field-type spans so missing-trait errors highlight the offending field.
    Errors for invalid items and trait impls in extra_constants blocks now correctly identify
    pallet::extra_constants instead of pallet::call. No source changes or storage migration
    are required.
crates:
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: patch
